@startuml recent-loss-handoff-sequence
title Position Consumer — Signal-Loss Episode Handoff (CP1)

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #CCCCCC
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

participant "Position Consumer\n(consumer.ts)" as PC #DBEAFE
participant "Redis" as Redis #FEF9C3

== Accepted resume position arrives ==

PC -> Redis : HGETALL alert-state:{entity_id}
Redis --> PC : dark_since_ms, signal_loss_alert_id, composite_issued

note right of PC
  If alert-state has no dark_since_ms,
  the entity was never dark — no-op,
  clearSignalLossEpisode returns immediately.
end note

== Entity was dark — close the episode ==

group MULTI / EXEC — one atomic transaction
  PC -> Redis : HSET recent-loss:{entity_id}\n  dark_since_ms, resumed_at_ms, signal_loss_alert_id
  PC -> Redis : PEXPIRE recent-loss:{entity_id} COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS
  PC -> Redis : DEL alert-state:{entity_id}
end
Redis --> PC : [1, 1, 1]  (all three applied)

note right of Redis
  No other client can observe an in-between
  state: recent-loss is never visible without
  its TTL already attached, and alert-state is
  never "half deleted" mid-handoff.
end note

== Crash boundary ==

note over PC, Redis
  Crash before EXEC reaches Redis: none of the three
  commands ran — alert-state is untouched, safe retry
  on the next accepted position for this entity.

  EXEC reaches Redis: all three ran — recent-loss has
  its TTL and alert-state is already gone. No window
  where EXEC succeeded but alert-state is still stale.
end note

@enduml
